WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:12.721 --> 00:00:14.097
What were you doing in Mexico?

00:00:15.974 --> 00:00:16.850
Oh, okay.

00:00:17.684 --> 00:00:18.977
A couple of people have been doing that.

00:00:18.977 --> 00:00:21.813
Here's an essential part of entry
with the summer upon us.

00:00:21.855 --> 00:00:23.898
We have high traffic, a lot of crossers.

00:00:24.065 --> 00:00:27.068
So we're seeing an increase of narcotics
smuggling, people

00:00:27.068 --> 00:00:28.153
smuggling.

00:00:35.452 --> 00:00:38.121
COVID played a big role
with human smuggling.

00:00:38.204 --> 00:00:41.374
Most of our smugglers are tourists
come from Mexico.

00:00:41.875 --> 00:00:45.462
So when they're were restricted from
entering the country during the pandemic,

00:00:45.670 --> 00:00:48.673
a lot of organizations
look towards United States citizens

00:00:48.798 --> 00:00:51.801
to try and smuggle people

00:00:58.058 --> 00:00:59.142
Hi. Good morning.

00:00:59.142 --> 00:01:02.103
Whenever we have people
crossing every day.

00:01:02.103 --> 00:01:04.898
99% of those people
there are legitimate travel.

00:01:05.190 --> 00:01:08.318
But we have people
that will get documents in Mexico.

00:01:08.318 --> 00:01:11.988
Either they buy the documents
or they steal the documents

00:01:11.988 --> 00:01:14.407
and they present themselves
as that person.

00:01:14.407 --> 00:01:16.409
Hi. Look in the camera.

00:01:16.409 --> 00:01:20.914
So this facial recognition system,
it's an extra layer of enforcement for us.

00:01:20.914 --> 00:01:24.834
To determine, one, that the person is
the person that she is presented.

00:01:25.001 --> 00:01:26.086
Do you mind just taking the mask off?

00:01:26.086 --> 00:01:28.421
I'm going to take a picture.
And also help us

00:01:28.421 --> 00:01:31.508
determine their citizenship
when they presented US passport

00:01:33.593 --> 00:01:34.260
Good afternoon.

00:01:34.260 --> 00:01:35.762
Buenas tardes.

00:01:37.889 --> 00:01:38.765
Okay.

00:02:07.836 --> 00:02:08.294
Subject

00:02:08.294 --> 00:02:11.548
presented a California driver's license

00:02:11.548 --> 00:02:13.842
as her indentification.

00:02:15.301 --> 00:02:17.470
When we did the biometrics
facial comparison,

00:02:17.595 --> 00:02:21.224
the picture did not match the picture
that she probably has

00:02:21.224 --> 00:02:25.395
with her US passport
so she was referred to secondary.

00:02:25.395 --> 00:02:28.815
So we can verify that
that's the person within.

00:02:30.733 --> 00:02:31.276
How are you, ma'am?

00:02:31.693 --> 00:02:33.778
Okay. Have you had a U.S. passport?

00:02:34.529 --> 00:02:36.072
Okay. Well.

00:02:36.114 --> 00:02:37.240
What happened to your passport?

00:02:42.704 --> 00:02:43.454
Okay.

00:03:02.348 --> 00:03:05.018
She was very straightforward,
always was looking at me.

00:03:05.059 --> 00:03:08.146
She didn't hesitate on responding
when we told her that we were going

00:03:08.146 --> 00:03:09.689
to take the fingerprint.

00:03:11.900 --> 00:03:14.903
That's usually a sign
that a person is being truthful

00:03:21.367 --> 00:03:22.535
We took her fingerprints

00:03:22.535 --> 00:03:24.913
and we corroborate that it was her.

00:03:25.705 --> 00:03:28.416
Thank you for your cooperation
and you're good to go.

00:03:28.750 --> 00:03:29.667
Have a good one.

